// Authored tactical points for bots.
//
// Registers per-map "good places to hold" into the engine's bot tactical memory
// (BotTacticalMemory). Bots that are NOT in combat pick the best reachable point
// of their team within 2048 units, walk there, hold it, and fight from it.
//
// This does NOT drive bots from script. The engine already owns the whole
// occupy/hold/release lifecycle (combat leash, return timeout, path-failure
// bailout, grenade avoidance). We only supply better candidate positions than
// the ones bots discover on their own.
//
// ## When does a bot actually go to a point?
//
// Every frame the engine checks, and a bot commits only if ALL hold:
//   - not on the 10-30s cooldown after leaving a previous point
//   - not already dwelling at a point
//   - NOT currently fighting        <- bots never abandon a firefight for a point
//   - not investigating a noise
//   - not avoiding a grenade
//   - a same-team, unoccupied, pathable point exists within 2048 units,
//     unused for the last 10s
//
// So camping emerges BETWEEN engagements. Points further than 2048u from where
// bots actually roam will never be picked.
//
// ## Authoring a point
//
// `bot_addtacticalpoint <standpos> <lookdir> <team>`
//   standpos - where the bot stands. Must be somewhere a player can actually
//              stand; use the `coord` console command while standing there.
//   lookdir  - direction the bot watches, as a vector (not angles). It is
//              normalized engine-side.
//   team     - "allies" or "axis". Points are per-team.
//
// Points are PINNED: bots learning spots at runtime can never evict them.
// They are level-scoped and cleared on map change, hence registration at init.
//
// Set `g_bot_debug_tactical_spots 1` to print each registered point plus the
// spots bots record on their own.
//
// Per-team budget is 16 points (MAX_SPOTS_PER_TEAM). Authored points count
// against it, so leave headroom for runtime learning.

main:
    if (level.tactical_initialized == 1) end
    level.tactical_initialized = 1

    local.preset = waitexec ("global/feho/tactical_presets/" + getcvar("mapname") + ".scr")

    if (local.preset != 1) {
        // No preset for this map: bots fall back to discovering spots themselves.
        end
    }
end
